    {
      "data": {
        "text": "<thinking> To create the file `aggregate_metric_stats.py` that retrieves aggregated statistics for a metric over a time window using a concrete external provider, I will choose Amazon CloudWatch as the provider. This is because CloudWatch is a widely used service for monitoring and retrieving metrics, and it provides a Python SDK that can be used to interact with the service. The code will import the necessary modules from the AWS SDK (Boto3) and use the CloudWatch client to retrieve the aggregated statistics. </thinking>\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789866469250,
          "start": 1789866465604
        },
        "type": "text"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc5ad944001jGXtk7kRaD7zAc",
      "message_id": "msg_0bc5ad4160012Ci8Puo4N0Fpvq",
      "session_id": "ses_f43a52bf9ffeb5yQ4gBcCbedj2",
